WEBVTT

00:03.690 --> 00:04.480
Okay.

00:04.970 --> 00:06.760
I'm going to junior college.

00:08.390 --> 00:11.200
I'll play properly at the 
audition. Don't worry.

01:42.730 --> 01:44.000
Tsukamoto.

01:44.000 --> 01:45.250
Take this, please.

01:45.250 --> 01:46.340
Thanks.

01:47.800 --> 01:50.490
I never would've thought camp 
prep would be such a pain.

01:47.800 --> 01:50.490
<i>I never would've thought camp 
prep would be such a pain.</i>

01:51.070 --> 01:55.260
<i>It makes you realize how 
capable our senpais were.</i>

01:55.260 --> 01:56.420
Get good.

01:55.260 --> 01:56.420
<i>Get good.</i>

01:56.420 --> 01:59.690
<i>I know it's a pain, but please don't 
dismiss him with a two-word answer.</i>

01:59.690 --> 02:00.900
Collect the membership fees!!

01:59.690 --> 02:00.900
<i>Collect the membership fees!</i>

02:00.900 --> 02:02.510
Those four words aren't much better.

02:00.900 --> 02:02.510
<i>Those four words aren't much better.</i>

02:05.290 --> 02:10.440
<i>After the Bon break, we have 
our three-day summer camp.</i>

02:10.880 --> 02:16.320
<i>It's not just the practices that heat 
up prior to the Kansai Competition.</i>

02:16.320 --> 02:17.590
<i>This year...</i>

02:20.270 --> 02:21.380
So...

02:21.380 --> 02:24.640
The audition is on the first night, right?

02:24.640 --> 02:25.620
That's right.

02:25.990 --> 02:28.870
Announcements will be on 
the morning of the second.

02:28.870 --> 02:30.440
R-Right.

02:30.790 --> 02:32.150
Here we go.

02:36.640 --> 02:41.020
<i>And so began three whirlwind days.</i>

02:42.850 --> 02:46.770
<b>Episode 8</b>

02:42.850 --> 02:46.770
<b>Melancholy Ostinato</b>

02:49.530 --> 02:52.370
Oh, watch your step there.

02:52.370 --> 02:53.030
Okay.

02:53.790 --> 02:57.510
We have this space rented out 
for the next three days.

02:57.510 --> 02:59.700
So you can leave the chairs out.

02:59.700 --> 03:02.950
Please arrange them as you would 
for our usual full ensembles.

03:02.950 --> 03:03.900
Right.

03:05.200 --> 03:06.470
Kumiko-chan.

03:07.530 --> 03:11.030
Hey, do we have specific arrangements 
for our meals and stuff?

03:11.370 --> 03:13.690
Nothing strict, I guess.

03:13.690 --> 03:16.060
Really? That's a relief.

03:16.060 --> 03:19.250
I'd get nervous with people I 
haven't talked to much before.

03:19.530 --> 03:20.450
Ah.

03:20.450 --> 03:22.740
I do like camps, though.

03:22.740 --> 03:24.920
It's a break from real life.

03:24.920 --> 03:28.010
Although, it does get dizzyingly busy.

03:29.620 --> 03:32.570
Let me know if there's 
anything I can help with.

03:33.510 --> 03:37.260
I'd do anything for you.

03:37.590 --> 03:39.220
Ah... Okay.

03:39.570 --> 03:40.930
Thanks.

03:40.930 --> 03:42.680
Well, see you later.

03:43.060 --> 03:43.890
Yeah.

03:44.560 --> 03:47.650
<i>She must have meant that.</i>

03:48.160 --> 03:50.100
<i>I could have just taken 
it at face value.</i>

03:51.130 --> 03:53.550
<i>That's what I told myself</i>

03:53.550 --> 03:57.330
<i>as I tried my best to ignore the 
nagging voice in the back of my mind.</i>

03:58.550 --> 04:00.170
<b>Main Sessional Room</b>

03:59.480 --> 04:04.750
Allow me to introduce the instructors 
who will be working with us this year.

04:05.830 --> 04:07.990
Hashimoto Masahiro.

04:07.990 --> 04:10.820
I'll be focusing on percussion.

04:10.820 --> 04:12.480
Feel free to talk to me about anything.

04:12.790 --> 04:14.540
I'm Niiyama Satomi.

04:14.540 --> 04:16.480
I'll be working with the winds.

04:16.800 --> 04:20.600
Let's try to get some results this year.

04:24.350 --> 04:28.740
Well then, let's split up 
for sectional practice.

04:29.300 --> 04:33.880
As I said before, the auditions for the 
Kansai Competition will happen tonight.

04:34.460 --> 04:37.870
Let's all do our best.

04:38.100 --> 04:39.020
Yes.

04:42.230 --> 04:47.130
Hearing that the audition is 
tonight makes my chest go oomf!

04:47.130 --> 04:49.080
It kind of reminds me of entrance exams.

04:49.080 --> 04:49.730
Please no.

04:50.210 --> 04:52.360
Plus, our results come 
in first thing tomorrow.

04:53.170 --> 04:54.910
I'm so tense!

04:54.910 --> 04:56.760
I don't think I can sleep tonight.

04:56.760 --> 04:59.660
We can just get all the tubas to perform!

04:59.660 --> 05:00.450
No way.

05:00.450 --> 05:02.120
There's five of you.

05:02.120 --> 05:05.980
I've seen about five tubas before.

05:05.980 --> 05:06.690
Really?

05:06.690 --> 05:08.360
I have, too.

05:08.360 --> 05:09.920
Most recently...

05:10.450 --> 05:12.450
Ryusei did it.

05:12.900 --> 05:14.580
Right, Tsukinaga-kun?

05:14.580 --> 05:15.920
We did.

05:15.920 --> 05:18.580
Grandpa likes having thick bass.

05:18.580 --> 05:19.930
Uh-huh.

05:19.930 --> 05:20.930
What?

05:20.930 --> 05:22.460
No. Nothing.

05:27.730 --> 05:29.590
That's Kousaka-senpai.

05:31.130 --> 05:32.870
The soli part.

05:48.340 --> 05:52.760
We can definitely make it to the Nationals 
if you and Kousaka-senpai play the soli.

05:52.760 --> 05:55.580
It's not like we can do it ourselves.

05:56.740 --> 05:59.850
Well, why don't we play 
together from the top?

06:00.650 --> 06:01.420
Okay.

06:07.480 --> 06:09.140
Be careful with the rhythm
in the bass section.

06:09.490 --> 06:13.090
Especially the syncopation in the third bar.

06:13.090 --> 06:13.970
Right.

06:13.970 --> 06:16.400
Marimba! This is your time to shine!

06:16.400 --> 06:17.450
You don't need to be shy.

06:17.450 --> 06:19.630
Demand to be seen!

06:19.630 --> 06:20.180
Okay!

06:20.720 --> 06:22.500
No slacking!

06:22.500 --> 06:25.400
Keep practicing it as many 
times as it takes to sink in.

06:25.400 --> 06:26.190
Yes.

06:26.480 --> 06:29.520
All right, let's all take 
it together from the top.

06:29.520 --> 06:30.540
Yes.

06:30.540 --> 06:31.580
Again!

06:31.580 --> 06:32.070
Yes!

06:32.070 --> 06:33.050
Again!

06:33.050 --> 06:33.790
Yes!

06:33.790 --> 06:34.650
Again!

06:34.920 --> 06:35.660
Yes!

06:35.660 --> 06:36.830
Again!

06:36.830 --> 06:40.180
Please, no more.

06:41.860 --> 06:44.280
I love curry!

06:44.850 --> 06:46.210
Kumiko-senpai.

06:46.570 --> 06:48.000
May I join you?

06:48.000 --> 06:49.300
Of course.

06:49.590 --> 06:51.870
Mayu-chan's coming soon, too.

06:51.870 --> 06:53.660
That's Kuroe-senpai for you.

06:53.660 --> 06:54.940
Never letting her guard down.

06:54.940 --> 06:56.100
There you go again.

06:56.100 --> 06:57.490
Am I wrong, though?

06:57.490 --> 07:01.810
I get the sense that you've 
kind of noticed it, too.

07:03.630 --> 07:04.920
Say what?

07:05.670 --> 07:09.280
Let a club into your heart, and bzzt!

07:09.280 --> 07:11.780
Mayu-chan's not like that.

07:11.780 --> 07:12.870
I made it.

07:12.870 --> 07:15.630
Sorry, I didn't know where the water was.

07:16.070 --> 07:17.250
Kanade-chan.

07:17.250 --> 07:18.500
I'll go get some more.

07:18.500 --> 07:20.160
No, it's fine.

07:20.160 --> 07:22.590
I can't have Kuroe-senpai fetch water.

07:24.610 --> 07:26.200
Don't mind her.

07:26.200 --> 07:28.400
She's like that to everyone.

07:28.400 --> 07:30.640
I like Kanade-chan.

07:30.640 --> 07:32.100
She's just brutally honest.

07:32.420 --> 07:36.010
I don't know if you'd call 
that "brutal honesty."

07:36.010 --> 07:38.440
Should we start eating?
We don't have much time.

07:38.440 --> 07:39.250
Okay.

07:40.200 --> 07:41.750
Let's eat.

07:41.750 --> 07:42.920
Let's eat.

07:44.730 --> 07:47.630
The audition's coming up, huh?

07:48.410 --> 07:49.410
Yeah.

07:53.050 --> 07:54.450
Kumiko-chan...

07:55.420 --> 07:56.370
Hm?

08:00.180 --> 08:02.900
Do you want to play the soli?

08:02.900 --> 08:04.540
Sure, if I can.

08:05.320 --> 08:06.430
Yeah...

08:11.570 --> 08:12.960
Mayu-chan?

08:18.570 --> 08:19.150
Mayu—

08:19.150 --> 08:21.970
Kumiko, do you have time after dinner?

08:21.970 --> 08:23.830
Yeah, why?

08:24.500 --> 08:26.520
Could you practice with me?

08:26.520 --> 08:29.050
I want to make sure we have the soli down.

08:29.050 --> 08:31.470
Oh, sure. Okay.

08:31.470 --> 08:32.820
Okay, talk to you later.

08:47.520 --> 08:48.490
Well?

08:48.490 --> 08:50.080
Yeah. We're good.

08:50.080 --> 08:51.890
I think it's better than before.

08:51.890 --> 08:53.810
Not me. You.

08:53.810 --> 08:54.260
Eh?

08:54.530 --> 08:58.720
Taki-sensei's been giving 
you more warnings lately.

08:58.720 --> 09:00.220
You think so?

09:00.220 --> 09:02.520
Not Kuroe-san, on the other hand.

09:03.180 --> 09:05.720
Mayu-chan's good, huh?

09:06.920 --> 09:09.180
I'm not sure she's good,
but she has good instincts.

09:09.840 --> 09:13.270
She immediately figures out what 
kind of sound Taki-sensei wants.

09:13.270 --> 09:15.580
And she produces that exact sound.

09:15.580 --> 09:17.650
I guess that's how you end 
up in Seira Girls' School.

09:17.650 --> 09:18.820
Just so you know...

09:21.360 --> 09:24.970
I intend on playing in 
the Nationals with you.

09:29.920 --> 09:31.000
Thanks.

09:42.550 --> 09:45.460
Maybe I'll practice one more time.

09:52.020 --> 09:53.530
Kumiko-chan.

09:53.530 --> 09:55.070
Going for a bath?

09:55.370 --> 09:56.180
Yeah.

10:12.710 --> 10:13.930
Kumiko-chan...

10:14.490 --> 10:17.680
Should I forfeit the audition?

10:22.390 --> 10:23.640
Why?

10:24.090 --> 10:26.630
You said you'd play.

10:26.630 --> 10:29.500
That's because you wanted me to.

10:29.500 --> 10:31.140
I still do.

10:33.100 --> 10:37.160
But you want to play the soli, don't you?

10:37.830 --> 10:42.110
Kousaka-san, Kanade-chan, and
 everyone think that's for the best, too.

10:42.710 --> 10:47.500
Still, it wouldn't be in Kitauji's 
best interest if you forfeit.

10:50.280 --> 10:51.620
Are you sure?

10:52.070 --> 10:54.390
I'm not that eager to play the soli.

10:54.390 --> 10:57.040
I just want to play with everyone.

10:58.080 --> 11:01.750
And everyone wants you to play.

11:01.750 --> 11:02.880
That's not right.

11:04.450 --> 11:06.270
I told you before.

11:06.690 --> 11:08.800
I want the best one to play.

11:10.020 --> 11:12.240
The best kids play.

11:12.700 --> 11:14.370
That's how Kitauji works.

11:17.690 --> 11:19.650
That's just you being polite!

11:20.530 --> 11:21.790
Think about it.

11:21.790 --> 11:23.860
A new kid transfers in,

11:23.860 --> 11:25.100
and takes the soli part away from

11:25.100 --> 11:26.960
the president who's been
working so hard all this time.

11:28.910 --> 11:33.390
Are you telling me you'd be 
chosen if you didn't forfeit?

11:34.720 --> 11:36.970
That's not what I meant.

11:41.460 --> 11:42.380
Sorry.

11:43.420 --> 11:44.320
Nah.

11:48.580 --> 11:53.810
Kitauji had this vibe when I entered, too.

11:54.210 --> 11:57.580
Like, "underclassmen should 
respect the upperclassmen."

11:57.580 --> 12:00.460
Or "the one who tried hardest 
should get the part."

12:04.020 --> 12:05.370
But it's changed.

12:06.420 --> 12:07.990
Didn't it get nasty?

12:07.990 --> 12:09.520
It did.

12:09.520 --> 12:12.400
But we worked hard to change it.

12:12.400 --> 12:14.370
That's why Kitauji is the way it is now.

12:14.800 --> 12:16.730
Everyone knows that.

12:17.670 --> 12:19.270
Are you sure?

12:19.270 --> 12:20.010
Yeah.

12:20.400 --> 12:22.010
That's Kitauji.

12:30.120 --> 12:31.150
All right.

12:34.480 --> 12:38.260
Sorry I took up your bath time.

12:42.440 --> 12:43.760
I'll see you later.

12:43.760 --> 12:44.660
Okay.

12:53.030 --> 12:54.210
Kumiko.

12:56.930 --> 12:58.400
Big news.

12:58.400 --> 12:59.510
What's up?

12:59.510 --> 13:02.490
Motomu-kun wants to talk to Midori.

13:03.550 --> 13:05.930
He said he had something 
important to tell me.

13:09.580 --> 13:12.180
Do you think it's what I think it is?

13:13.150 --> 13:14.810
So, what are you going to do?

13:15.840 --> 13:17.770
I'll go hear him out.

13:17.770 --> 13:19.390
Yeah. Figures.

13:21.070 --> 13:23.250
Sorry, I should get ready.

13:23.250 --> 13:24.970
Oh, that's right. Sorry.

13:24.970 --> 13:26.320
Good luck.

13:26.320 --> 13:27.160
Yeah.

13:28.020 --> 13:29.580
Kumiko-senpai.

13:29.580 --> 13:31.400
We were worried about you.

13:31.400 --> 13:33.110
You're first up.

13:33.110 --> 13:34.610
My bad.

13:38.130 --> 13:39.590
Sorry.

13:39.590 --> 13:41.950
You're practically late, Senpai.

13:41.950 --> 13:44.040
I took too long in the bath.

13:50.350 --> 13:51.250
Mayu-chan...

13:52.510 --> 13:54.960
Let's both do our best.

13:56.020 --> 13:58.520
<b>Main Sessional Room</b>

13:57.610 --> 14:01.150
<i>And so, the auditions proceeded as planned.</i>

14:03.570 --> 14:06.770
Euphonium. Third-year. Oumae Kumiko.

14:08.840 --> 14:12.000
Euphonium. Third-year. Kuroe Mayu.

14:14.930 --> 14:19.950
<i>Mayu-chan went ahead with the 
audition without forfeiting.</i>

14:19.330 --> 14:21.960
<b>Euphonium</b>

14:19.330 --> 14:21.960
<b>Oumae Kumiko</b>

14:19.330 --> 14:21.960
<b>Kuroe Mayu</b>

14:19.330 --> 14:21.960
<b>Hisaishi Kanade</b>

14:28.690 --> 14:29.830
That's refreshing.

14:29.830 --> 14:31.680
What, you're treating us?

14:31.680 --> 14:32.440
That's rare.

14:32.440 --> 14:34.410
No, it's from Taki-sensei.

14:34.980 --> 14:37.270
You should have said so!

14:40.690 --> 14:43.280
And the announcement's tomorrow.

14:43.280 --> 14:45.230
Everyone's going to be anxious.

14:46.320 --> 14:50.030
Do you think Taki-sensei plans on 
changing the section composition?

14:50.030 --> 14:52.070
I think it's possible.

14:52.680 --> 14:57.410
I guess euph or saxophone are 
on the chopping block, then.

14:57.920 --> 14:59.880
What do you think, Kousaka?

14:59.880 --> 15:02.910
That's up to Taki-sensei to decide.

15:02.910 --> 15:06.830
We simply do what we can to 
perform as Taki-sensei needs.

15:07.390 --> 15:10.360
That's the quickest way 
to winning National gold.

15:10.360 --> 15:11.760
I hope so.

15:11.760 --> 15:12.920
What's that supposed to mean?

15:13.220 --> 15:18.710
Well, some students definitely had 
questions about the Prefecturals.

15:18.710 --> 15:22.390
We could never perform properly if we 
kept worrying about every complaint.

15:22.390 --> 15:24.720
I get that.

15:24.720 --> 15:26.780
But given two people were equally capable,

15:26.780 --> 15:29.650
you can't help but want the 
third-year to have priority.

15:29.650 --> 15:31.890
You want him to play favorites just 
because it's their last time?

15:31.890 --> 15:35.710
No, I just said if they're 
"equally capable."

15:36.990 --> 15:39.350
So, what do you think, President?

15:41.050 --> 15:42.380
I...

15:42.860 --> 15:45.200
<i>Reina's right.</i>

15:45.200 --> 15:47.590
<i>It's the ideal. But...</i>

15:47.590 --> 15:51.790
So you aren't satisfied with 
this result either, then?

15:54.050 --> 15:54.800
No.

15:55.150 --> 15:57.320
I think Reina's right.

15:58.820 --> 16:01.060
Well, don't oversleep tomorrow.

16:01.380 --> 16:03.820
That's rich coming from Tsukamoto.

16:03.820 --> 16:05.000
Agreed.

16:06.590 --> 16:08.380
You haven't finished that?!

16:08.380 --> 16:08.980
Yeah.

16:09.330 --> 16:11.910
I'll cherish it later.

16:11.910 --> 16:14.300
S-So pure!

16:14.300 --> 16:14.900
Shut up!

16:14.900 --> 16:16.260
Ouch.

16:16.260 --> 16:17.540
Jeez.

16:17.540 --> 16:19.220
I'm complimenting you.

16:24.260 --> 16:25.590
Someone's there.

16:29.370 --> 16:31.910
You're not allowed to buy 
stuff after lights out.

16:31.910 --> 16:33.620
You are if you don't get caught.

16:33.620 --> 16:35.360
You bad girl.

16:36.570 --> 16:38.450
Someone's coming! Hurry!

16:38.450 --> 16:39.680
Wait!

16:40.030 --> 16:40.880
Bah!

16:56.820 --> 16:58.330
Puppy Waltz

17:01.870 --> 17:04.340
Hey, it's Midori-chan.

17:04.760 --> 17:06.990
Kumiko-chan. Reina-chan.

17:06.990 --> 17:08.010
What's wrong?

17:08.480 --> 17:11.030
I'm just having a hard time sleeping.

17:11.030 --> 17:12.520
Is something wrong?

17:16.100 --> 17:18.840
You knew, didn't you, Kumiko-chan?

17:18.840 --> 17:20.800
About Motomu-kun.

17:20.800 --> 17:22.280
Tsukinaga-kun?

17:22.280 --> 17:24.340
Oh, yeah, it's a thing.

17:25.870 --> 17:28.940
I couldn't stop thinking.

17:29.380 --> 17:31.470
And I just realized...

17:31.870 --> 17:35.500
People have all sorts 
of unexpected feelings.

17:37.710 --> 17:40.670
What did Motomu-kun tell you?

17:45.250 --> 17:46.550
I'm not telling you.

17:51.180 --> 17:52.260
Yeah?

17:52.550 --> 17:57.380
Still, I plan on being my normal 
self starting tomorrow.

17:57.380 --> 17:59.900
I think that's good, too.

17:59.900 --> 18:02.750
Kumiko, I'm heading back.

18:02.750 --> 18:03.820
Nah.

18:03.820 --> 18:05.570
Let's go back together, the three of us.

18:05.980 --> 18:07.030
Is that okay?

18:07.030 --> 18:08.940
Yeah, let's go back.

18:10.340 --> 18:13.430
Kawashima-san, you can 
have this if you want.

18:13.430 --> 18:15.040
Really?

18:15.040 --> 18:15.910
Yeah.

18:15.910 --> 18:17.950
Reina-chan's a goddess!

18:17.030 --> 18:19.600
<i>I've come to think lately...</i>

18:20.280 --> 18:24.380
<i>That there are some things you're 
just better off not knowing.</i>

18:54.230 --> 18:56.280
Oh, yeah...

18:56.700 --> 18:59.790
This is my last camp.

19:03.160 --> 19:06.910
Sound! Euphonium

19:06.040 --> 19:06.910
To
Oumae Kumiko-sama
#302 Maison Kisen
935 Ujitougawa, Uji-shi, Kyoto-fu

From
Tanaka Asuka
#302 Aparupare Kamogawa
Asago Ryugu Kita-hairu, 
Kamigyou-ku, 
Kyoto-shi, Kyoto-fu

19:06.910 --> 19:10.670
To
Oumae Kumiko-sama
#302 Maison Kisen
935 Ujitougawa, Uji-shi, Kyoto-fu

From
Tanaka Asuka
#302 Aparupare Kamogawa
Asago Ryugu Kita-hairu,
 Kamigyou-ku, Kyoto-shi, Kyoto-fu

20:08.550 --> 20:12.480
Since when have you two been so close?

20:13.710 --> 20:15.500
It's more like,

20:15.500 --> 20:18.950
I was going to practice on my own this 
morning, but Suzume-chan was there.

20:19.380 --> 20:22.120
I can't let Satsuki-senpai beat me!

20:23.480 --> 20:25.920
Did your exec meeting last night run late?

20:25.920 --> 20:27.150
Did you get any sleep?

20:27.150 --> 20:29.570
I heard you were up early this morning, too.

20:29.570 --> 20:31.200
Yeah, I manage.

20:32.310 --> 20:35.940
You're worried for Kumiko-chan, huh?

20:35.940 --> 20:42.790
I guess. It's just that Kumiko-senpai likes 
to draw the short straw if you let her.

20:42.790 --> 20:44.850
Oh, come on. No way.

20:44.850 --> 20:46.250
Really, though?

20:46.250 --> 20:49.710
I thought you just liked being 
a bleeding-heart altruist.

20:51.900 --> 20:53.730
Oh, shoot, the time...

20:53.730 --> 20:55.500
Sorry, I should get going.

20:55.890 --> 20:57.470
Take care.

20:57.810 --> 20:59.690
That must be so tough.

20:59.690 --> 21:02.070
The announcements are at eight, too.

21:02.070 --> 21:05.440
I hope all of us get to play 
together at the competition.

21:06.670 --> 21:08.460
Do you honestly mean that?

21:08.830 --> 21:10.150
Of course.

21:10.150 --> 21:11.070
Why not?

21:12.830 --> 21:16.190
Never mind. That was a silly 
question to ask you, Kuroe-senpai.

21:20.090 --> 21:24.600
I'll hereby announce the 
results of the audition.

21:24.950 --> 21:29.360
Having a different roster each 
competition is a first for Kitauji.

21:29.940 --> 21:35.850
It may be difficult, but I'm hopeful 
that it'll have been for the best.

21:37.350 --> 21:39.190
Well, here I go.

21:39.640 --> 21:40.850
First, the trumpets.

21:41.190 --> 21:43.480
Third-year, Kousaka Reina-san.

21:43.480 --> 21:44.400
Yes.

21:44.400 --> 21:46.440
Second-year, Kohinata Yume-san.

21:46.440 --> 21:47.160
Yes.

21:47.160 --> 21:49.370
Third-year, Yoshizawa Akiko-san.

21:47.600 --> 21:49.580
<i>Come to think of it,</i>

21:49.370 --> 21:49.980
Yes.

21:49.580 --> 21:55.830
<i>this was the first time Taki-sensei read 
out the performing members himself.</i>

21:51.130 --> 21:52.440
Trombones.

21:52.440 --> 21:54.810
Third-year, Tsukamoto Shuichi-kun.

21:54.810 --> 21:55.730
Yes.

21:56.300 --> 21:57.270
Oboes.

21:56.810 --> 22:02.230
<i>Those members had their names called 
out as I was pondering that fact.</i>

21:57.270 --> 21:59.410
Second-year, Kenzaki Ririka-san.

21:59.410 --> 22:00.330
Yes.

22:02.490 --> 22:04.380
Next, euphoniums.

22:05.290 --> 22:07.510
Third-year, Oumae Kumiko-san.

22:07.510 --> 22:08.290
Yes.

22:08.290 --> 22:10.310
Third-year, Kuroe Mayu-san.

22:10.310 --> 22:11.020
Yes.

22:11.020 --> 22:12.600
Those are our two.

22:13.750 --> 22:15.150
Next, tubas.

22:15.440 --> 22:17.630
Third-year, Katou Hazuki-san.

22:17.630 --> 22:19.040
Y-Yes.

22:19.040 --> 22:21.000
Second-year, Suzuki Mirei-san.

22:21.000 --> 22:21.400
Yes.

22:21.770 --> 22:23.560
Second-year, Suzuki Satsuki-san.

22:23.560 --> 22:24.520
Y-Yes.

22:24.910 --> 22:26.820
First-year, Kamaya Suzume-san.

22:26.820 --> 22:27.990
Yes.

22:27.990 --> 22:29.440
Those are our four tubas.

22:31.140 --> 22:34.540
Now, I'll announce our soloists.

22:36.510 --> 22:41.160
For the selection piece, clarinet, 
third-year, Takashita Chieri-san.

22:41.160 --> 22:41.790
Yes.

22:41.790 --> 22:45.160
Contrabass, third-year, 
Kawashima Sapphire-san.

22:45.160 --> 22:45.800
Yes.

22:46.040 --> 22:48.970
Marimba, third-year, Kamaya Tsubame-san.

22:48.970 --> 22:49.790
Yes.

22:49.790 --> 22:53.310
Trumpet, third-year, Kousaka Reina-san.

22:53.310 --> 22:54.050
Yes.

22:54.360 --> 22:56.690
Euphonium, third-year,

22:57.010 --> 22:58.300
Kuroe Mayu-san.

23:03.750 --> 23:04.650
Yes.

23:15.540 --> 23:16.770
<i>And so...</i>

23:18.480 --> 23:21.040
<i>the next piece begins.</i>

23:22.000 --> 23:25.960
<b>To be continued</b>
